<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francisco Félix de Souza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1754–1849</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Chacha</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francisco Félix de Souza was a Brazilian slave trader who became the most powerful merchant at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ouidah">Ouidah</a>, the main port of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-dahomey">Kingdom of Dahomey</a>. He helped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghezo">Ghezo</a> seize the throne from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adandozan">Adandozan</a> in 1818 and received the title of chacha, making him the king's agent for trade with Europeans. He amassed great wealth from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic slave trade</a>, and his descendants remain prominent in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francisco-felix-de-souza.jpg" alt="Francisco Félix de Souza" width="320" height="385" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Francisco_F%C3%A9lix_de_Souza.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
